{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared canonicalisation vectors for the BNM Lab remote-support signature (contract 2.4).",
    "Rule: object keys sorted recursively by UTF-16 code unit, arrays in order, no whitespace,",
    "numbers exactly as sent (the bridge writes them with JSON.stringify; the app re-emits the",
    "parsed literal unchanged), strings JSON-escaped with lowercase \\uXXXX for control characters,",
    "non-ASCII raw. sha256 is over the UTF-8 bytes of `canonical`.",
    "TRAP: JSON.stringify of a re-keyed JS object puts integer-like keys (\"9\", \"10\") first in numeric",
    "order — the bridge must build the canonical string by hand (see the 'key order' vector).",
    "Loaded by composeApp/src/desktopTest/.../remote/CanonicalJsonTest.kt AND tools/remote-mcp/test/canonical.test.mjs —",
    "same input must give the same canonical string and hash on both sides. Regenerate only by running",
    "both suites; never hand-edit a canonical/sha256 value."
  ],
